text:
claire: Starting a tiny docs cleanup: split the big function/tool-calling page into three micro-snippets so other READMEs can link to exact examples. Keeping everything short and copyable.

matt: Agree. Proposed anchors: #snippet-invoke-call, #snippet-output-schema, #snippet-parse-fallback. Use kebab-case and avoid generated ids.

zayn: I'll author the JSON schema snippet. Keep it minimal (required props only), include explicit types, and a small example of a tool returning an extra field. Example payload to show: `{
  "id": 42,
  "result": "OK",
  "meta": { "duration_ms": 120 }
}` then schema matches only id and result.

matt: I'll do the split/anchors PR. My changes will be limited to headings and code fences and wrapping examples with the snippet component placeholders.

claire: For SDK examples include both major flavors. Short migration note above the snippets: "If you are upgrading SDK major versions, prefer the labeled snippet for your version." Label 3.x and 4.x examples.

zayn: Quick schema note: prefer "type": "integer" for id, and set "nullable": false for required fields. Example shim I will show: `const { id, result } = response; // ignore meta`

matt: For TS snippet I'll use this minimal example and wrap it with the Snippet component in the markdown:```ts
const res = await client.invoke({
  name: 'summarize',
  input: { text: longText }
});
console.log(res.output);
```
Keep under ~15 lines.

claire: Add a one-line parse-fallback sentence under the fallback snippet: "Fallback order: strict JSON -> tolerant JSON -> regex fallback." Also include a tiny CLI smoke test demonstrating a strict parse fail then fallback success.

docs-bot: deploy-preview available at https://deploy-preview.redwood/docs/invoke-micro-snippets-4932 (CI lint passed) :white_check_mark:

matt: Timeline: open small focused PRs by Friday EOD. Prefix PR titles with `docs: micro invoke snippets`. I'll open the split/anchor PR tomorrow morning.

zayn: Schema PR by Thursday EOD with the shim example and explicit example output.

claire: Great. When opening PRs add a one-line changelog entry in the PR body and run the page link-checker. If any cross-page broken links appear, escalate and run site-wide checker. Tag me on PRs.

matt: Will do. Tagging @claire when I open.

zayn: Thanks all 44d
